  "id": "1lb544z",
  "title": "Chapter 19: President of India",
  "order": 20,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0ahb06a",
      "content": "The President of India is the constitutional head of the country and the first citizen of India. All executive actions of the Government of India are carried out in the name of the President. The office of the President is described in Part V of the Constitution (Articles 52–62)."
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
